  "bio_summary": "Mirabai Chanu Saikhom, born on August 8, 1994, is an Indian weightlifter who has achieved significant international success. She rose to prominence by winning a silver medal at the 2020 Tokyo Olympics in the women's 49 kg event, becoming only the second Indian weightlifter to win an Olympic medal. Chanu has also secured multiple medals at the World Championships and Commonwealth Games, demonstrating consistent performance at the elite level. Her journey from a humble background in Manipur to a global stage has made her one of India's most celebrated athletes.",
